Z||000007||sqoach||11-10-2001||05:18 PM||||What about the oxygen sensor? Also could be a vacuum leak, as avengador1 said.<P>Do you still have your stock exhaust? I'd check for a clogged converter.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">                <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||11-10-2001||05:49 PM||||Pull the rubber boot that connects the throttle body to the air filter off. You should be able to see a hole just in front of the throttle blade inside the bore of the throttle body. With the engine running, cover that hole with your finger. If the engine RPM's drop, I'd say you have a bad IAC or a bad connection between the IAC and computer. If covering the hole doesn't change things, then you have a major vac leak. Check where the pipe comes from the intake to the back of the throttle body- it gets pulled out sometimes and check where the power brake connects to the plenum.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BC-GT||11-10-2001||06:56 PM||||Can we assume that you have moved the timing mark to the proper location, the 2.8 and 3.4 have the marks in two completely different spots. Is the whole motor rebuilt, or just new sensors and accessories?<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||crypto1079||11-11-2001||09:25 AM||||No, it's not rebuilt.  Low-mileage 3.4.  <BR>New sensors, this engine was modified by ed parks.  Yes, new timing mark was cut.  The only thing I did was have some machine work done to the heads and intakes.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||crypto1079||11-11-2001||09:34 AM||||Yes, as previously mentioned, I replaced the oxygen sensor already.  I do not have a clogged exhaust for sure.  Had both cat and muffler replaced already.  I have also extensively checked for vacuum leaks.  I replaced all intake gaskets, egr tube, egr valve, and vacuum lines. I have also tried plugging the brake booster vacuum port and the evaporation canister/cruise control vacuum ports.  No change.  When I plug the iac port in the TB, the engine dies.  What does this mean?  Thanks.<BR>  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||11-11-2001||12:21 PM||||What is your BLM and Integrator? Are the injectors too big? I had a similar problem with mine when I was using the 17-lb. hour 3.4 injectors. When I got my scan tool I discovered that the BLM was 120 and the integrator was dipping down to 20 at idle and part throttle conditions at low speeds. The injectors were too big! I changed the injectors to blueprinted 2.8 injectors, turned up the fuel pressure to 47 psi and now the idle is more stable and it doesn’t run rich anymore. I runs a whole lot better now.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||crypto1079||11-11-2001||12:37 PM||||BLM and Integrator?  Never heard of either of those terms.  However, I am not running rich, I am running lean, which is really wierd.  If anything, I would think I would be running rich.  I am using 19# injectors (302), with about 48 psi pressure. I don't think that 19# is too much for this engine though.  It is a 3.4, and I have had my intake and heads gasket matched.  I recently have gotten code 22 (TPS), so I have one on order now, hopefully this will help.  From what I understand, a faulty TPS could cause lean conditions.<P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||88formula||11-11-2001||10:12 PM|||| I have ported heads, performance valve job with SI valves. A GM performance camshaft and FOCOA headers and my engine ran rich with the 17 lb. an hour injectors!<P>In short the BLM is the long term fuel strategy and the integrator is the short term. 128 is the norm. Any number above that and the computer is adding fuel. Any number below that and the computer is taking fuel away.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||crypto1079||11-12-2001||12:28 AM||||Ok, rich I would be happy with.  But why, with 19# injectors, am I still running lean?  That is my question...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||3.2SHO||11-12-2001||02:13 AM||||88Formula you still selling that car?||||reg||1
Z||000017||Formula||11-12-2001||01:21 PM||||your almost always going to run rich with the stock fiero intake, ported or not.<P>it just can flow the air that you need to run anything over 17# injectors.  Now if you switch to cooters dual tb setup, you can probably run 24# injectors without running rich.<P>right now I have the stock intake and exhaust on a 3.4 crate motor and it runs rich, it will run out of air at around 4500 rpms so its not much of a tp end monster.<P>I would check the cat and then move onto the vacuum lines<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Untitled-1_copy.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||crypto1079||11-12-2001||01:35 PM||||I replaced my cat with straight pipe and installed rodney dickman's steel vacuum lines.  Again, these items are new:<BR>exhaust, iac valve, vacuum lines, egr valve, egr tube, air charge sensor, coolant temp sensor, ign coil, pickup coil, ign module, dist cap and rotor, plugs, wires, intake gaskets, fuel pump (high flow), fuel filter, fuel regulator (adjustable, set at 48 psi), pcv valve.  I still run lean.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Alex4mula||11-12-2001||02:12 PM||||Your problem could be so many things. I had an idle problem for one year until I swaped TPS sensors with other car. Scanner didn't show up nothing noticeable. Anyway, I 100% agree with 88Formula. I have very similar setup with no lean problems. With stock PROM you may have issues with your fuel setup. I have to disagree that you need 19# inj. and 48psi for your engine. But you could have it and run OK with a reprogrammed PROM.<BR>Any bad sensor could make the computer crazy including causing lean conditions. Do you have a scanner? I think you will need one to further diagnose this. I know how frustrating this could be. And replacing parts could get very expensive. How far are you from West Palm Beach? I may be able to help you.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
